          #TheProcessOfModalities.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Passing to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triples"} adjoint triples
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+monads"} idempotent monads
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+comonads"} idempotent comonads
              which this induces, then yields
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  on the left the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape modality
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∫
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+modality"} flat modality
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ♭
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat
                  and
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sharp+modality"} sharp modality
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo ♯
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sharp
              %li
                %p
                  in the middle yields the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduction+modality"} reduction modality
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℜ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Re
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+shape+modality"} infinitesimal shape modality
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℑ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Im
                  and the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+flat+modality"} infinitesimal flat modality
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi &amp;
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \&amp;
              %li
                %p
                  on the right we get an adjoint triple whose whose middle bit
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⇝
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rightsquigarrow
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+modality"} bosonic modality
                  and whose left piece
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⇉
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rightrightarrows
                  produces
                  %em super-even
                  components, containing all the “
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermion"} fermion
                  = succeed "\u201D" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/currents"} currents
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unity+of+opposites"} unity of opposites
                  hence deserves to be called the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermionic+modality"} fermionic modality
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Rh
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rh
                  is the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rheonomy+modality"} rheonomy modality
            %p
              Hence we get a process of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+modalities"} adjoint modalities
